{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And every meal-offering of a priest.</b> For if it were not entirely consumed, it would say ״shall not eat — the remainder.״ For what gift is there before the Place [i.e., HaShem] like the handful that he scoops, which is but a small thing? With an Israelite who brings a meal-offering, he brings a tenth [of an ephah], and the handful is burned and the remainder is eaten by the priests — and the priests acquire from the High Table, so the whole of it is a gift. But with that of a priest, if he were to eat the remainder, it would not be a gift. And it is not like the sin-offerings and guilt-offerings of priests, for there the fat and the portions are burned, with the hides [going] to the men of the watch."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:50.728117149Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}